{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"374b66c8225eceb1","name":"card_event_regia_aeronautica","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/events/card_event_regia_aeronautica","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"REGIA AERONAUTICA","text":"Deal damage to each enemy equal to friendly air units.","flavorText":"The Regia Aeronautica was established in 1923, following the creation of the Kingdom of Italy's unified air force. Over the years, it developed into a key component of Italy's military forces, participating in various conflicts, including the Spanish Civil War (1936–1939). During WWII the air force played a vital role in supporting the country's military campaigns from 1940 to 1943. Initially, it was well-equipped with modern aircraft, such as the Macchi C.200 and Fiat G.50 fighters, but it struggled later against superior Allied forces. In the Mediterranean theater, it battled British and Commonwealth forces, particularly during the North African Campaign, where it provided air support for ground operations in Libya and Egypt. Despite its strengths in some areas, the Regia Aeronautica faced critical issues, including outdated training, inferior aircraft later in the war, and a lack of coordination with the Italian Army and Navy. The air force's initial successes were overshadowed by heavy losses due to the technological superiority of Allied aircraft like the Spitfire and P-40. After Italy's surrender in 1943, the Regia Aeronautica was split, with some units joining the Allies (forming Kingdom of Italy’s Co-belligerent Air Force) and others aligning with the German Luftwaffe (forming Italian Social Republic’s National Republican Air Force).","faction":"Italy","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_regia_aeronautica","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_regia_aeronautica_title","SourceString":"REGIA AERONAUTICA","LocalizedString":"REGIA